Chapter: Fireworks
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 USA 250 -- fireworks bursting over a major American city skyline,
 rendered on the bare-metal host GPU triangle rasterizer. The guest
 composes a screen-space triangle command buffer in RAM at 0xBE000000
 and fires I/O port 0x400; codex-vm rasterizes it at native speed into
 the GOP framebuffer, with an atmosphere-glow bloom pass for free.

 Stage 2: a live particle simulation. Shells launch from the rooftops,
 arc upward under gravity, and explode into radial bursts of sparks
 that fall and fade over their lifetime. Particles live in a fixed
 flat RAM buffer (poke/peek, O(1), zero per-frame heap allocation).

 We say:

Section: Constants

  cmd-buf : Integer = #BE000000
  sw : Integer = 1024
  sh : Integer = 768
  horizon : Integer = 680
  kb-addr : Integer = 28680
  max-tri : Integer = 60000
  city-seed : Integer = 777

  num-cities : Integer = 5
  frames-per-city : Integer = 600
  finale-len : Integer = 900
  cycle-cities : Integer = num-cities * frames-per-city
  cycle-total : Integer = cycle-cities + finale-len
  force-city : Integer = -1
  force-finale : Integer = 0

  part-base : Integer = #B0000000
  part-cap : Integer = 2600
  part-stride : Integer = 32
  gravity : Integer = 20
  launch-every : Integer = 9
  burst-count : Integer = 150
  sim-substeps : Integer = 3
  burst-alt : Integer = 170

 Particle field byte offsets within a 32-byte slot. Position and
 velocity are fixed-point at 1/256 pixel.

  f-px : Integer = 0
  f-py : Integer = 4
  f-vx : Integer = 8
  f-vy : Integer = 12
  f-life : Integer = 16
  f-max : Integer = 20
  f-col : Integer = 24
  f-kind : Integer = 28

Section: Colors

  sky-top : Integer = #060616
  sky-horizon : Integer = #2A1840
  fade-sky : Integer = #04040E
  water-top : Integer = #180C28
  water-bottom : Integer = #05030A
  building-col : Integer = #141634
  shell-col : Integer = #FFF0C0

  landmark-col : Integer = #1C2148
  antenna-col : Integer = #C83A2A
  gg-orange : Integer = #C0442A
  gg-cable : Integer = #8A2F1E
  needle-col : Integer = #2A3060
  monument-col : Integer = #D8D2C0
  dome-col : Integer = #C8C4B4
  trans-col : Integer = #6A6E86

  burst-color : Integer -> Integer
  burst-color (k) =
    let m = k - (k / 6) * 6
    in if m == 0 then #FF3324
    else if m == 1 then #FFFFFF
    else if m == 2 then #3A6BFF
    else if m == 3 then #FFD028
    else if m == 4 then #46E070
    else #C64BFF

Section: Triangle Primitives

 A triangle is 72 bytes in the command buffer: three screen xy pairs,
 three packed XRGB per-vertex colors, three depths, then six texture
 coords at zero. Winding gives a negative signed area so the rasterizer
 keeps the face. Small depth values draw in front; the sky/water use
 large depths as the backdrop.

  put-tri3 : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  put-tri3 (cmd) (idx) (x0) (y0) (x1) (y1) (x2) (y2) (c0) (c1) (c2) (d) =
    let o = idx * 72
    in let w0 = poke-32 cmd o x0
    in let w1 = poke-32 cmd (o + 4) y0
    in let w2 = poke-32 cmd (o + 8) x1
    in let w3 = poke-32 cmd (o + 12) y1
    in let w4 = poke-32 cmd (o + 16) x2
    in let w5 = poke-32 cmd (o + 20) y2
    in let w6 = poke-32 cmd (o + 24) c0
    in let w7 = poke-32 cmd (o + 28) c1
    in let w8 = poke-32 cmd (o + 32) c2
    in let w9 = poke-32 cmd (o + 36) d
    in let wa = poke-32 cmd (o + 40) d
    in let wb = poke-32 cmd (o + 44) d
    in let wc = poke-32 cmd (o + 48) 0
    in let wd = poke-32 cmd (o + 52) 0
    in let we = poke-32 cmd (o + 56) 0
    in let wf = poke-32 cmd (o + 60) 0
    in let wg = poke-32 cmd (o + 64) 0
    in let wh = poke-32 cmd (o + 68) 0
    in idx + 1

  put-rect : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  put-rect (cmd) (idx) (x) (y) (w) (h) (col) (d) =
    if idx >= max-tri then idx
    else let i1 = put-tri3 cmd idx x y x (y + h) (x + w) y col col col d
    in put-tri3 cmd i1 (x + w) y x (y + h) (x + w) (y + h) col col col d

  put-quad-c : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  put-quad-c (cmd) (idx) (x) (y) (w) (h) (ctop) (cbot) (d) =
    if idx >= max-tri then idx
    else let i1 = put-tri3 cmd idx x y x (y + h) (x + w) y ctop cbot ctop d
    in put-tri3 cmd i1 (x + w) y x (y + h) (x + w) (y + h) ctop cbot cbot d

 put-tri3-add / put-rect-add tag the triangle for additive blending by
 storing 1 in the first texcoord slot; codex-vm cinematic mode reads that
 flag and sums the fragment into the framebuffer instead of overwriting,
 so overlapping sparks build hot, bloom-able cores.

  put-tri3-add : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  put-tri3-add (cmd) (idx) (x0) (y0) (x1) (y1) (x2) (y2) (c0) (c1) (c2) (d) =
    let o = idx * 72
    in let w0 = poke-32 cmd o x0
    in let w1 = poke-32 cmd (o + 4) y0
    in let w2 = poke-32 cmd (o + 8) x1
    in let w3 = poke-32 cmd (o + 12) y1
    in let w4 = poke-32 cmd (o + 16) x2
    in let w5 = poke-32 cmd (o + 20) y2
    in let w6 = poke-32 cmd (o + 24) c0
    in let w7 = poke-32 cmd (o + 28) c1
    in let w8 = poke-32 cmd (o + 32) c2
    in let w9 = poke-32 cmd (o + 36) d
    in let wa = poke-32 cmd (o + 40) d
    in let wb = poke-32 cmd (o + 44) d
    in let wc = poke-32 cmd (o + 48) 1
    in let wd = poke-32 cmd (o + 52) 0
    in let we = poke-32 cmd (o + 56) 0
    in let wf = poke-32 cmd (o + 60) 0
    in let wg = poke-32 cmd (o + 64) 0
    in let wh = poke-32 cmd (o + 68) 0
    in idx + 1

  put-rect-add : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  put-rect-add (cmd) (idx) (x) (y) (w) (h) (col) (d) =
    if idx >= max-tri then idx
    else let i1 = put-tri3-add cmd idx x y x (y + h) (x + w) y col col col d
    in put-tri3-add cmd i1 (x + w) y x (y + h) (x + w) (y + h) col col col d

 put-sprite draws a SOFT round additive glow: a quad tagged u0=2 with the
 sprite center (cx,cy) and radius stored in the texcoords, so codex-vm
 cinematic mode shades each fragment with a radial falloff. Combined with
 bloom this reads as a real luminous ember instead of a hard square.

  put-tri3-soft : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  put-tri3-soft (cmd) (idx) (x0) (y0) (x1) (y1) (x2) (y2) (col) (cx) (cy) (r) =
    let o = idx * 72
    in let w0 = poke-32 cmd o x0
    in let w1 = poke-32 cmd (o + 4) y0
    in let w2 = poke-32 cmd (o + 8) x1
    in let w3 = poke-32 cmd (o + 12) y1
    in let w4 = poke-32 cmd (o + 16) x2
    in let w5 = poke-32 cmd (o + 20) y2
    in let w6 = poke-32 cmd (o + 24) col
    in let w7 = poke-32 cmd (o + 28) col
    in let w8 = poke-32 cmd (o + 32) col
    in let w9 = poke-32 cmd (o + 36) 300
    in let wa = poke-32 cmd (o + 40) 300
    in let wb = poke-32 cmd (o + 44) 300
    in let wc = poke-32 cmd (o + 48) 2
    in let wd = poke-32 cmd (o + 52) 0
    in let we = poke-32 cmd (o + 56) cx
    in let wf = poke-32 cmd (o + 60) cy
    in let wg = poke-32 cmd (o + 64) r
    in let wh = poke-32 cmd (o + 68) 0
    in idx + 1

  put-sprite : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  put-sprite (cmd) (idx) (sx) (sy) (r) (col) =
    if idx >= max-tri then idx
    else let x0 = sx - r
    in let y0 = sy - r
    in let x1 = sx + r
    in let y1 = sy + r
    in let i1 = put-tri3-soft cmd idx x0 y0 x0 y1 x1 y0 col sx sy r
    in put-tri3-soft cmd i1 x1 y0 x0 y1 x1 y1 col sx sy r

Section: Sky and Water

  draw-sky : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-sky (cmd) (idx) = put-quad-c cmd idx 0 0 sw horizon sky-top sky-horizon 9000

  draw-water : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-water (cmd) (idx) = put-quad-c cmd idx 0 horizon sw (sh - horizon) water-top water-bottom 8600

Section: Procedural Skyline

  hsh : Integer -> Integer
  hsh (n) = bit-and (bit-shru ((n * 1103515245) + 12345) 16) 1023

  draw-city : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-city (cmd) (idx) (bx) (seed) =
    if bx >= sw then idx
    else if idx >= max-tri then idx
    else let bw = 44 + (hsh (bx + seed)) * 46 / 1024
    in let bh = 90 + (hsh (bx * 3 + seed + 11)) * 340 / 1024
    in let top = horizon - bh
    in let i2 = put-rect cmd idx bx top bw bh building-col 700
    in let cols = (bw - 12) / 12
    in let rows = (bh - 18) / 14
    in let i3 = draw-windows cmd i2 bx top bw bh (bx + seed) 0 cols rows
    in draw-city cmd i3 (bx + bw + 7) seed

  draw-windows : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-windows (cmd) (idx) (bx) (top) (bw) (bh) (seed) (k) (cols) (rows) =
    if cols <= 0 then idx
    else if rows <= 0 then idx
    else if k >= cols * rows then idx
    else if idx >= max-tri then idx
    else let cc = k - (k / cols) * cols
    in let rr = k / cols
    in let lit = bit-and (hsh (bx + k * 31 + seed)) 7
    in if lit >= 3 then draw-windows cmd idx bx top bw bh seed (k + 1) cols rows
    else let wx = bx + 6 + cc * 12
    in let wy = top + 10 + rr * 14
    in let wcol = if bit-and (hsh (bx + k * 7 + seed)) 1 == 0 then #FFD070 else #BFD8FF
    in let i2 = put-rect cmd idx wx wy 6 8 wcol 650
    in draw-windows cmd i2 bx top bw bh seed (k + 1) cols rows

Section: Landmarks

 Recognizable American skylines. Each city draws a procedural backdrop
 for depth, then its signature landmark(s) in front at a smaller depth.
 Every triangle lists the left base vertex, then the right base, then the
 apex (for an apex-up shape), giving the negative signed area the
 rasterizer keeps; apex-down shapes list the right base first.

  draw-skyline : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-skyline (cmd) (idx) (city) =
    if city == 0 then draw-nyc cmd idx
    else if city == 1 then draw-chicago cmd idx
    else if city == 2 then draw-sf cmd idx
    else if city == 3 then draw-seattle cmd idx
    else draw-dc cmd idx

  draw-nyc : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-nyc (cmd) (idx) =
    let i0 = draw-city cmd idx 0 101
    in draw-empire cmd i0 512

  draw-empire : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-empire (cmd) (idx) (cx) =
    let i1 = put-rect cmd idx (cx - 60) (horizon - 300) 120 300 landmark-col 500
    in let i2 = put-rect cmd i1 (cx - 44) (horizon - 372) 88 72 landmark-col 490
    in let i3 = put-rect cmd i2 (cx - 28) (horizon - 430) 56 58 landmark-col 480
    in let i4 = put-rect cmd i3 (cx - 8) (horizon - 500) 16 70 landmark-col 470
    in put-tri3 cmd i4 (cx - 5) (horizon - 500) (cx + 5) (horizon - 500) cx (horizon - 542) antenna-col antenna-col antenna-col 460

  draw-chicago : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-chicago (cmd) (idx) =
    let i0 = draw-city cmd idx 0 203
    in draw-willis cmd i0 512

  draw-willis : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-willis (cmd) (idx) (cx) =
    let i1 = put-rect cmd idx (cx - 80) (horizon - 300) 160 300 landmark-col 500
    in let i2 = put-rect cmd i1 (cx - 80) (horizon - 372) 104 72 landmark-col 495
    in let i3 = put-rect cmd i2 (cx - 40) (horizon - 420) 80 48 landmark-col 490
    in let i4 = put-rect cmd i3 (cx - 30) (horizon - 470) 24 50 landmark-col 485
    in let i5 = put-rect cmd i4 (cx + 6) (horizon - 470) 24 50 landmark-col 485
    in let i6 = put-rect cmd i5 (cx - 20) (horizon - 512) 4 42 antenna-col 480
    in put-rect cmd i6 (cx + 14) (horizon - 512) 4 42 antenna-col 480

  draw-sf : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-sf (cmd) (idx) =
    let i0 = draw-city cmd idx 0 307
    in let i1 = draw-transamerica cmd i0 800
    in draw-goldengate cmd i1 380 644

  draw-transamerica : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-transamerica (cmd) (idx) (cx) =
    let i1 = put-rect cmd idx (cx - 6) (horizon - 120) 12 120 trans-col 505
    in put-tri3 cmd i1 (cx - 30) (horizon - 120) (cx + 30) (horizon - 120) cx (horizon - 400) trans-col trans-col trans-col 505

  draw-goldengate : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-goldengate (cmd) (idx) (lx) (rx) =
    let ttop = horizon - 340
    in let i1 = put-rect cmd idx (lx - 12) ttop 24 (horizon - ttop) gg-orange 450
    in let i2 = put-rect cmd i1 (rx - 12) ttop 24 (horizon - ttop) gg-orange 450
    in let i3 = put-rect cmd i2 (lx - 12) (ttop + 40) 24 14 gg-orange 445
    in let i4 = put-rect cmd i3 (rx - 12) (ttop + 40) 24 14 gg-orange 445
    in let i5 = put-rect cmd i4 lx (horizon - 150) (rx - lx) 8 gg-orange 448
    in draw-cable cmd i5 lx ttop (rx - lx) 130 0

  draw-cable : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-cable (cmd) (idx) (x0) (topy) (span) (sag) (i) =
    if i > 24 then idx
    else let u = i * 2 - 24
    in let px = x0 + i * span / 24
    in let yy = topy + sag - sag * u * u / 576
    in let i2 = put-rect cmd idx (px - 1) yy 3 3 gg-cable 440
    in draw-cable cmd i2 x0 topy span sag (i + 1)

  draw-seattle : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-seattle (cmd) (idx) =
    let i0 = draw-city cmd idx 0 411
    in draw-needle cmd i0 512

  draw-needle : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-needle (cmd) (idx) (cx) =
    let i1 = put-tri3 cmd idx (cx - 60) horizon (cx - 30) horizon (cx - 6) (horizon - 280) needle-col needle-col needle-col 500
    in let i2 = put-tri3 cmd i1 (cx + 30) horizon (cx + 60) horizon (cx + 6) (horizon - 280) needle-col needle-col needle-col 500
    in let i3 = put-rect cmd i2 (cx - 6) (horizon - 280) 12 280 needle-col 498
    in let i4 = put-rect cmd i3 (cx - 48) (horizon - 306) 96 20 needle-col 490
    in let i5 = put-tri3 cmd i4 (cx + 48) (horizon - 286) (cx - 48) (horizon - 286) cx (horizon - 274) needle-col needle-col needle-col 490
    in let i6 = put-rect cmd i5 (cx - 4) (horizon - 344) 8 38 needle-col 488
    in put-tri3 cmd i6 (cx - 4) (horizon - 344) (cx + 4) (horizon - 344) cx (horizon - 362) antenna-col antenna-col antenna-col 486

  draw-dc : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-dc (cmd) (idx) =
    let i0 = draw-city cmd idx 0 523
    in let i1 = draw-monument cmd i0 400
    in draw-capitol cmd i1 660

  draw-monument : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-monument (cmd) (idx) (cx) =
    let i1 = put-rect cmd idx (cx - 13) (horizon - 430) 26 430 monument-col 500
    in put-tri3 cmd i1 (cx - 13) (horizon - 430) (cx + 13) (horizon - 430) cx (horizon - 462) monument-col monument-col monument-col 498

  draw-capitol : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-capitol (cmd) (idx) (cx) =
    let i1 = put-rect cmd idx (cx - 90) (horizon - 70) 180 70 dome-col 500
    in let i2 = put-rect cmd i1 (cx - 52) (horizon - 112) 104 42 dome-col 498
    in let i3 = put-rect cmd i2 (cx - 34) (horizon - 150) 68 38 dome-col 496
    in let i4 = put-tri3 cmd i3 (cx - 34) (horizon - 150) (cx + 34) (horizon - 150) cx (horizon - 188) dome-col dome-col dome-col 494
    in put-rect cmd i4 (cx - 2) (horizon - 204) 4 16 dome-col 492

Section: Glyph Font

 A 3x5 bitmap font. Each glyph is 15 bits: five rows of three columns,
 row-major from the top, column 0 the most significant. A set bit draws
 one sz-by-sz block via the rasterizer at depth 150 so text sits in front
 of the particles. Only the letters and digits the labels need are
 defined.

  g-a : Integer = 11245
  g-c : Integer = 14627
  g-d : Integer = 27502
  g-e : Integer = 31143
  g-f : Integer = 31140
  g-g : Integer = 14699
  g-h : Integer = 23533
  g-i : Integer = 29847
  g-k : Integer = 23469
  g-l : Integer = 18727
  g-n : Integer = 24573
  g-o : Integer = 11114
  g-r : Integer = 27565
  g-s : Integer = 14478
  g-t : Integer = 29842
  g-u : Integer = 23407
  g-w : Integer = 23549
  g-y : Integer = 23186
  g-d0 : Integer = 31599
  g-d1 : Integer = 11415
  g-d2 : Integer = 29671
  g-d5 : Integer = 31183
  g-d6 : Integer = 31215
  g-d7 : Integer = 29330
  g-m : Integer = 24557
  g-p : Integer = 27556
  g-b : Integer = 27566
  g-bang : Integer = 9346
  g-dash : Integer = 448
  g-dot : Integer = 128

  draw-glyph : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-glyph (cmd) (idx) (x) (y) (sz) (col) (bits) = draw-glyph-px cmd idx x y sz col bits 0

  draw-glyph-px : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-glyph-px (cmd) (idx) (x) (y) (sz) (col) (bits) (i) =
    if i >= 15 then idx
    else let row = i / 3
    in let cp = i - row * 3
    in let mask = bit-shl 1 (14 - i)
    in if bit-and bits mask == 0 then draw-glyph-px cmd idx x y sz col bits (i + 1)
    else let i2 = put-rect cmd idx (x + cp * sz) (y + row * sz) sz sz col 150
    in draw-glyph-px cmd i2 x y sz col bits (i + 1)

  gc : Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  gc (cmd) (idx) (x0) (y) (sz) (col) (k) (bits) =
    draw-glyph cmd idx (x0 + k * sz * 4) y sz col bits

Section: Labels

 The persistent chrome: the anniversary banner across the top and the
 current city's name beneath it. Drawn every frame from immediate glyph
 constants, so no heap allocation and no fixed-RAM text table.

  banner-col : Integer = #FFD028
  name-col : Integer = #FFFFFF
  seahawks-col : Integer = #69BE28
  band-y : Integer = 36
  name-y : Integer = 84
  txt-sz : Integer = 5

  draw-banner : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-banner (cmd) (idx) =
    let x0 = 322
    in let b = band-y
    in let s = txt-sz
    in let i0 = gc cmd idx x0 b s banner-col 0 g-u
    in let i1 = gc cmd i0 x0 b s banner-col 1 g-s
    in let i2 = gc cmd i1 x0 b s banner-col 2 g-a
    in let i4 = gc cmd i2 x0 b s banner-col 4 g-d2
    in let i5 = gc cmd i4 x0 b s banner-col 5 g-d5
    in let i6 = gc cmd i5 x0 b s banner-col 6 g-d0
    in let i8 = gc cmd i6 x0 b s banner-col 8 g-dot
    in let i10 = gc cmd i8 x0 b s banner-col 10 g-d1
    in let i11 = gc cmd i10 x0 b s banner-col 11 g-d7
    in let i12 = gc cmd i11 x0 b s banner-col 12 g-d7
    in let i13 = gc cmd i12 x0 b s banner-col 13 g-d6
    in let i14 = gc cmd i13 x0 b s banner-col 14 g-dash
    in let i15 = gc cmd i14 x0 b s banner-col 15 g-d2
    in let i16 = gc cmd i15 x0 b s banner-col 16 g-d0
    in let i17 = gc cmd i16 x0 b s banner-col 17 g-d2
    in gc cmd i17 x0 b s banner-col 18 g-d6

  draw-city-name : Integer, Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-city-name (cmd) (idx) (city) =
    if city == 0 then draw-name-nyc cmd idx
    else if city == 1 then draw-name-chicago cmd idx
    else if city == 2 then draw-name-sf cmd idx
    else if city == 3 then draw-name-seattle cmd idx
    else draw-name-dc cmd idx

  draw-name-nyc : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-name-nyc (cmd) (idx) =
    let x0 = 432
    in let y = name-y
    in let s = txt-sz
    in let i0 = gc cmd idx x0 y s name-col 0 g-n
    in let i1 = gc cmd i0 x0 y s name-col 1 g-e
    in let i2 = gc cmd i1 x0 y s name-col 2 g-w
    in let i4 = gc cmd i2 x0 y s name-col 4 g-y
    in let i5 = gc cmd i4 x0 y s name-col 5 g-o
    in let i6 = gc cmd i5 x0 y s name-col 6 g-r
    in gc cmd i6 x0 y s name-col 7 g-k

  draw-name-chicago : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-name-chicago (cmd) (idx) =
    let x0 = 442
    in let y = name-y
    in let s = txt-sz
    in let i0 = gc cmd idx x0 y s name-col 0 g-c
    in let i1 = gc cmd i0 x0 y s name-col 1 g-h
    in let i2 = gc cmd i1 x0 y s name-col 2 g-i
    in let i3 = gc cmd i2 x0 y s name-col 3 g-c
    in let i4 = gc cmd i3 x0 y s name-col 4 g-a
    in let i5 = gc cmd i4 x0 y s name-col 5 g-g
    in gc cmd i5 x0 y s name-col 6 g-o

  draw-name-sf : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-name-sf (cmd) (idx) =
    let x0 = 382
    in let y = name-y
    in let s = txt-sz
    in let i0 = gc cmd idx x0 y s name-col 0 g-s
    in let i1 = gc cmd i0 x0 y s name-col 1 g-a
    in let i2 = gc cmd i1 x0 y s name-col 2 g-n
    in let i4 = gc cmd i2 x0 y s name-col 4 g-f
    in let i5 = gc cmd i4 x0 y s name-col 5 g-r
    in let i6 = gc cmd i5 x0 y s name-col 6 g-a
    in let i7 = gc cmd i6 x0 y s name-col 7 g-n
    in let i8 = gc cmd i7 x0 y s name-col 8 g-c
    in let i9 = gc cmd i8 x0 y s name-col 9 g-i
    in let i10 = gc cmd i9 x0 y s name-col 10 g-s
    in let i11 = gc cmd i10 x0 y s name-col 11 g-c
    in gc cmd i11 x0 y s name-col 12 g-o

  draw-name-seattle : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-name-seattle (cmd) (idx) =
    let x0 = 442
    in let y = name-y
    in let s = txt-sz
    in let i0 = gc cmd idx x0 y s name-col 0 g-s
    in let i1 = gc cmd i0 x0 y s name-col 1 g-e
    in let i2 = gc cmd i1 x0 y s name-col 2 g-a
    in let i3 = gc cmd i2 x0 y s name-col 3 g-t
    in let i4 = gc cmd i3 x0 y s name-col 4 g-t
    in let i5 = gc cmd i4 x0 y s name-col 5 g-l
    in let i6 = gc cmd i5 x0 y s name-col 6 g-e
    in draw-seahawks-line cmd i6

 The 12th-Man sub-line, Seattle only. HOME OF THE REIGNING SUPERBOWL
 CHAMPION SEAHAWKS! in action green, drawn at half the city-name size on
 its own row. Column indices leave a blank slot for each word break.

  draw-seahawks-line : Integer, Integer -> Integer
  draw-seahawks-line (cmd) (idx) =
    let x0 = 218
    in let y = 118
    in let s = 3
    in let c = seahawks-col
